I'd consider that a "non-fighting" character in what I posted earlier. BTW 
sticking with a class and choosing the same one each game makes a *huge* 
difference in your learning and survivability. The difference between 
classes is easily sufficient for that to be true.

In addition learn a) what monsters you *can* safely melee with - there are 
some very dangerous exceptions that people die from *all* the time and b) 
what ones you can safely eat and what if any benefits happens when you do. 
You *will* get a one line message when this happens. Somewhat cryptic 
perhaps, but you get one.

Also learn what weapons you can use that a) you can enchant your skill the 
most and b) do the most damage. And then avoid enhancing any others as much 
as possible in the early game.


